body:
This PR removes the `white` parameter from the shader binary objects, but  #110671 requires this parameter to be included in the binary objects for use with the new screen glow blending behaviour. If it looks like #110671 will be merged, I can adapt this PR to make sense with the new screen glow blending behaviour.

I've also made a small update to the tonemap parameters to better use the "or_greater" property hint:
``` c++
ADD_PROPERTY(PropertyInfo(Variant::FLOAT, "tonemap_exposure", PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE, "0,4.0,0.01,or_greater"), "set_tonemap_exposure", "get_tonemap_exposure");
ADD_PROPERTY(PropertyInfo(Variant::FLOAT, "tonemap_white", PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE, "0.01,16.0,0.01,or_greater"), "set_tonemap_white", "get_tonemap_white");
ADD_PROPERTY(PropertyInfo(Variant::FLOAT, "tonemap_contrast", PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE, "1.0,2.0,0.01,or_greater"), "set_tonemap_contrast", "get_tonemap_contrast");
```

(When I made this PR, I wasn't aware of the "or_greater" property hint 😅)

Edit: Checks are failing after rebase because the version has been bumped up to 4.6. I'll need to re-do the `extension_api_validation` work for this 4.6 update at some point...
